From: George Watson <george@hellas.ai>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: add `nocamera` build tag to exclude libkvm.so

`libkvm.so` (the vendor cgo dep behind `common/kvm_vision.go`)
registers ~20 C++ static constructors in its `.init_array`. They run
at process startup -- before main(), before any Go code, before our
prior IsHdmiDisabled guard can even see the disk. One of them calls
`SAMPLE_COMM_VI_ParseIni` -> `_try_release_sys`, which dereferences a
NULL sensor descriptor on mainline kernels (no vendor sensor INI
present) and SEGVs the whole server.

Source-level guards can't help; we have to keep libkvm.so out of the
link entirely. Add a `nocamera` build tag:

  go build -tags nocamera ./...

The cgo file `kvm_vision.go` gets `//go:build !nocamera`. A new
`kvm_vision_stub.go` with `//go:build nocamera` provides no-op
implementations of the same API (KvmVision, GetKvmVision, ReadMjpeg,
ReadH264, SetHDMI, SetGop, SetFrameDetect, Close). Building with
-tags nocamera selects the stub file, the cgo file is excluded, no
-lkvm in LDFLAGS, no .so is dlopened, no constructors fire.

The server boots cleanly; HDMI capture / video streaming endpoints
return errors (-1) but HID, network, storage, OLED-config, auth, and
the rest of the web UI work normally.

Vendor-kernel builds (which actually have working camera capture)
build without -tags nocamera and keep the original cgo path.
---
diff -urN a/server/common/kvm_vision.go b/server/common/kvm_vision.go
--- a/server/common/kvm_vision.go
+++ b/server/common/kvm_vision.go
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+//go:build !nocamera
+
 package common

 /*
diff -urN a/server/common/kvm_vision_stub.go b/server/common/kvm_vision_stub.go
--- a/server/common/kvm_vision_stub.go
+++ b/server/common/kvm_vision_stub.go
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+//go:build nocamera
+
+// Stub for kvm_vision when built without the vendor camera SDK. The
+// real file (kvm_vision.go) links libkvm.so via cgo; that library's
+// .init_array registers ~20 C++ static constructors which call into
+// SAMPLE_COMM_VI_ParseIni and dereference a NULL sensor descriptor on
+// mainline kernels (no vendor sensor INI present). The constructors
+// run at process startup before any Go code, so we can't guard
+// around them — we have to keep libkvm.so out of the link entirely.
+//
+// Building with -tags nocamera selects this file and excludes the
+// real one, so the server starts with no HDMI capture / video
+// streaming but everything else (HID, network, storage, OLED-config,
+// auth, web UI) works.
+
+package common
+
+import (
+	"sync"
+
+	log "github.com/sirupsen/logrus"
+)
+
+var (
+	kvmVision     *KvmVision
+	kvmVisionOnce sync.Once
+)
+
+type KvmVision struct{}
+
+func GetKvmVision() *KvmVision {
+	kvmVisionOnce.Do(func() {
+		kvmVision = &KvmVision{}
+		log.Debugf("kvm vision: built with -tags nocamera; HDMI capture unavailable")
+	})
+	return kvmVision
+}
+
+func (k *KvmVision) ReadMjpeg(width uint16, height uint16, quality uint16) (data []byte, result int) {
+	return nil, -1
+}
+
+func (k *KvmVision) ReadH264(width uint16, height uint16, bitRate uint16) (data []byte, result int) {
+	return nil, -1
+}
+
+func (k *KvmVision) SetHDMI(enable bool) int {
+	return 0
+}
+
+func (k *KvmVision) SetGop(gop uint8) {}
+
+func (k *KvmVision) SetFrameDetect(frame uint8) {}
+
+func (k *KvmVision) Close() {}
